{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Vendor alias map for the TOOLING page's documented-case-mention counts:",
    "every vendor named in a tooling_map.json 'examples' array gets one entry",
    "per category it appears in — canonical display name (verbatim the",
    "examples string), category id, and the alias strings that identify the",
    "product in prose. The scanner (apps/search/vendor_mentions.py) counts",
    "DISTINCT case documents whose stored text matches any alias — presence",
    "in the record, never an effectiveness score, and NEVER an input to the",
    "category ranking math (tests pin byte-identity).",
    "",
    "MATCHING SEMANTICS: case-insensitive, word-boundary — an alias matches",
    "only when not butted against another letter/digit on either side, and",
    "multi-word aliases tolerate any whitespace run between words. Matching",
    "is one compiled alternation, longest alias first, so a more specific",
    "product name shadows a shorter prefix at the same position ('Proofpoint",
    "ITM' credits the ITM entry, not the bare 'Proofpoint' email entry —",
    "unqualified 'Proofpoint' elsewhere in the text still counts for email).",
    "",
    "ALIAS SAFETY RULES (tests/test_vendor_mentions.py enforces):",
    "1. An alias must be specific enough that a match in a court filing",
    "   almost certainly refers to the product. Single common English words",
    "   are FORBIDDEN as bare aliases — court prose is full of 'sterling',",
    "   'archer', 'relativity', 'hid', 'sans', 'purview' ('within the purview",
    "   of'), 'sentinel', 'falcon', 'canary', 'encase' (the verb), 'group",
    "   policy' (group insurance policies). Those vendors use compound",
    "   aliases ('RSA Archer', 'HID Global', 'Sterling background check',",
    "   'Windows Group Policy', 'Purview eDiscovery') instead.",
    "2. Single-token aliases are allowed ONLY from single_token_allowlist",
    "   below: coined brand names with no common-English collision",
    "   (CrowdStrike, Teramind, ObserveIT, Okta, ...). 'Velociraptor' is a",
    "   documented judgment call: a species name, but implausible as",
    "   non-product prose in an insider-case corpus. Multi-word aliases must",
    "   be at least 6 characters.",
    "3. When no safe alias exists, the entry keeps an EMPTY alias list plus a",
    "   'no_safe_alias' note so the vendor can never miscount ('Intune device",
    "   control': any real mention says 'Intune', which names the platform —",
    "   claimed by the Microsoft Intune entry under hardening).",
    "4. A company token shared across category entries belongs to its",
    "   flagship entry only (bare 'Proofpoint' -> email; bare 'SentinelOne'",
    "   -> edr; bare 'Splunk' -> siem; bare 'Intune' -> hardening); sibling",
    "   entries use product-qualified compounds or well-known former product",
    "   names (ObserveIT, Wombat Security, Attivo, Splunk UBA).",
    "5. Well-known FORMER names count as aliases (ObserveIT, Websense, Vontu,",
    "   Azure Active Directory, Google Chronicle, Bomgar, Thycotic, Centrify,",
    "   Lumension, kCura, Guidance Software, Attivo, Wombat Security) — old",
    "   court records name products by the name of their era.",
    "6. Same product legitimately homed in two categories (Netskope: dlp and",
    "   casb) carries the same aliases in both entries; a mention counts for",
    "   both homes."
  ],
